Troubleshooting
Symptom	Likely Cause	Fix
No PWM output	MOE bit not set in TIM16 BDTR	Ensure TIM16->BDTR = 0x8000 in initTimer16().
Encoder not counting	Wrong alternate function for pins	Verify PA0 and PB3 are configured as Alternate Function 1 (AF1).
Buzzer always silent	TIM6 interrupt disabled	Check NVIC ISER1 bit 22 (IRQ 54) is enabled.
LED always off	Constant overspeed condition or GPIO error	Verify the speed_rpm calculation and PB5 mode.
Fan not spinning at 100%	PWM frequency mismatch	Ensure TIM16 ARR=3199 for 25kHz, as required by the 4-wire fan spec.
Display blank	SPI initialization failure or power	Check display power (3.3V) and SPI connections (PA5, PA7, PA4, etc.).

Safety Notes
Hearing Protection: The buzzer produces a 500 Hz tone at full volume during overspeed. Avoid prolonged exposure during testing.

Voltages: The system uses a 12V supply for the fan. Ensure all connections are secure to prevent short circuits.

Fan Safety: Keep objects away from the fan blades while the system is powered.

Current Limits: The LED is current-limited by a 330Ω resistor. Do not connect the LED without a current-limiting resistor.

